"windowHints.explanationSettings" = "Hint mode: each thumbnail shows a key sequence; type it to focus that window. Single-letter hints are ordered: right-hand home row, then the rest of the right hand, then left-hand home row, then the rest of the left hand, then digits. The key bound to “Close the switcher immediately” is never used as a hint, and that shortcut only closes the switcher while window-hint mode is on (not in normal navigation after Escape). With window hints off in preferences, “Close the switcher immediately” works whenever the switcher is open. If you assign the same key to “Close the switcher” and “Quit app” without modifiers, it closes the switcher only in hint mode and quits the app in normal navigation. Escape leaves hint mode and restores normal navigation. While the search field is focused, hints are paused; Tab moves focus to thumbnails for hints, then Tab again returns to search. When search is locked, hints match the filtered list. Vim keys are configured in “Shortcuts when active…”. Shortcuts that switch between hint modes (minimize, close, quit, fullscreen, hide) are configured in “Additional controls…” under Hint mode navigation. Requires “After keys are released” set to “Keep open” while this option is on.";
